All changes are complete. Here's a summary of what was done:

**Files changed:**
- `Game Design Document/Gameplay Rules/Terminology.md` — major ECS terminology update
- `Game Design Document/Overview/Terminology.md` — updated redirect description
- `.ralph-tui/progress.md` — documented learnings and patterns

**Key changes to Terminology.md:**
1. **New ECS Architecture section** — defines Entity (ID), Component (data), System (logic), and archetype (common Component set)
2. **Entities** — reframed as unique IDs with no inherent data; all properties come from Components
3. **Tags** — reframed as "marker Components" with Entity Tag / Status Tag categories
4. **Zones** — reframed as state Components managed by the Zone System (not "used like Tags")
5. **Game object archetypes** — Commander, Army, Battleforce, Unit, Model, Item all described with their characteristic Component sets
6. **Combat Resolution** — reframed as the Combat System pipeline with Attack Pipeline (reads attacker Components, produces Damage Instances) and Defense Pipeline (reads target Components, consumes Damage Instances); downstream Systems (Morale, Ability) observe results
7. **Morale, Speed, Abilities, Keywords** — all updated to reference Components and their respective Systems
8. **Cross-references** — verified alignment with Entity System Rules (200–270) and Battle Rules (100–150)

All changes are uncommitted for manual review.

